title: 7. Each building mission carries out one part of the plan, and is done when that part's check passes, with the evidence shown.
pid: a76dc8ee-8d76-4a73-a5f5-6333ed26a605
body: |2-
  Top's mission links the plan and names the part; it does not restate it.
  The builder does not change a decision silently. Where the code
  shows a decision wrong, it edits the decision where it stands and
  says why; if that passes a one-way door, it stops and says so in
  its 'to Claude'.
  It marks its part built in the plan only when the check passes, and
  puts the command it ran and what it printed in its report.
  Before stopping, it has a fresh subagent, which never saw its
  reasoning, compare its changes with its part of the plan, skipping
  style. That is the check against the plan, and it costs no mission.
  Top reads the builder's 'to Claude' and the plan's state, not the code.
  Rests on: read (Anthropic's long-running harnesses: agents declare
  victory early, so a part is marked passing only after testing it
  as a user would, and the list of parts is not edited by the
  builders; Claude Code's best practices: ask for evidence, and
  review against the spec in a fresh subagent).
